                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Choose the Growth Mode`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `The rival's AI launch forced the board's hand. You have three mutually exclusive paths to ship AI demand-forecasting before the <strong>31 May 2027 cliff</strong>: <strong>acquire NordCast</strong> (€95M, owns the IP and talent now), <strong>ally</strong> with the same NordCast (€25M, fast and reversible but no IP ownership), or <strong>build</strong> in-house (€35M, full control but ships in 20–24 months). Score them against speed to the cliff, cost and value at risk, control of IP, and reversibility — then name the <em>single factor</em> that decides it. Remember: <strong>€16M of ARR renews before a build ships</strong>, and the boldest mode is not automatically the value-maximizing one.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Value the Deal & Test the Synergy`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Put numbers on your path. The €95M asking price is <strong>9.5x NordCast's €10M revenue</strong> for a pre-profit firm — justified entirely by synergy you must now size. Build the bridge: how much credible <em>revenue synergy</em> (cross-sell the AI module into your base), how much <em>cost synergy</em>, net of integration spend — against the <strong>€12M floor</strong>. A diligence finding lands: the lead architect built 40% of the model and has no lock-in. Then make the call: go, adjust, or walk. Over-promise the synergy bridge and you buy the <strong>winner's curse</strong>.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Set Integration Depth & the Cultural-Fit Plan`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Design the post-deal operating model. Set <strong>integration depth</strong> on the preservation→absorption spectrum, choose a talent-retention and cultural-fit plan for the <strong>60 research-led engineers</strong>, and pick the mechanism that actually captures the synergy. Here is the central tension: deep, fast integration accelerates the €12M synergy <em>but</em> historically triggers <strong>30–50% engineer attrition</strong> — and the value you bought <em>is</em> the talent. Lose them and the synergy is fiction. Ring-fence them entirely and you preserve the culture but forfeit the synergy. Find the depth that protects the people and still moves the number.`,
